## Prerequisites

- Terraform 1.3 or newer
- Google Cloud CLI (`gcloud`)
- The Compute Engine API enabled in `{{project_id}}`{{#if enable_private_link}}, plus the Cloud DNS API{{/if}}
- The caller granted `roles/iam.serviceAccountTokenCreator` on `{{google_service_account_email}}`
- `{{google_service_account_email}}` with project permissions required to create the VPC, subnets,{{#if enable_private_link}} PSC endpoints, DNS,{{/if}} networking resources, and Databricks workspace
- The same service account added to the Databricks account and assigned the Account Admin role
- `{{databricks_admin_user}}` already present as a Databricks account user

Enable the required GCP API:

```bash
gcloud services enable compute.googleapis.com{{#if enable_private_link}} dns.googleapis.com{{/if}} --project {{project_id}}
```

## Authenticate

Configure the project and impersonate the service account used by both Terraform providers. See [service account impersonation](https://cloud.google.com/docs/authentication/use-service-account-impersonation).

```bash
gcloud config set project {{project_id}}
gcloud config set auth/impersonate_service_account {{google_service_account_email}}
export GOOGLE_OAUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN="$(gcloud auth print-access-token)"
```

The access token is intentionally not stored in `terraform.tfvars`. Refresh it if Terraform reports that it has expired.

## Deploy

```bash
terraform init
terraform validate
terraform plan
terraform apply
```

After deployment:

```bash
terraform output -raw workspace_url
```

## Resources created

{{#if enable_private_link}}
The deployment creates a VPC, node and PSC subnets with Private Google Access, two Back-end PSC endpoints, private DNS records, a Databricks MWS network and private access settings, a workspace, and workspace admin membership. {{#if enable_nat_gateway}}Cloud Router and Cloud NAT provide general outbound connectivity.{{else}}Cloud NAT is disabled, so workloads need an alternate route for general internet egress.{{/if}}

The generated configuration does not assign a Unity Catalog metastore. The PSC service attachments are selected for `{{region}}`; confirm current regional values in the [Databricks regional infrastructure documentation](https://docs.databricks.com/gcp/en/resources/ip-domain-region#psc) before deployment.
{{else}}
The deployment creates a VPC, a subnet with Private Google Access, Cloud Router, Cloud NAT, a Databricks MWS network, a workspace, and workspace admin membership. Databricks creates the workspace cloud-storage buckets.

This deployment does not configure Private Service Connect or Unity Catalog.
{{/if}}

## Destroy

```bash
terraform destroy
```

If the VPC remains in use by Databricks-managed firewall rules, complete the Databricks workspace teardown before retrying.

